      "path": "assets/fig/p03_3.png",
      "y0": 187.71078491210938,
      "y1": 262.3966369628906,
      "caption": "Figure 2. Vector field results from different coupling strate- gies. Random coupling forces the model to regress inconsistent (gray) velocity targets, creating ambiguous intersections and push- ing the model toward an averaged (purple) direction, which pro- duces curved velocity fields. In contrast, optimal transport provides consistent couplings with fewer intersections, enabling the model to learn much straighter velocity fields.",
      "label": "Figure 2",
      "w": 670,
      "h": 618
    },
    {
